Decouple the command layer's dialogs from the GTK control.

Seven places reachable from a generic WorkbookControl cast it to WBCGtk
without a type check (docs/architecture.md section 5), so a Cocoa control
would crash on the error, confirmation, and progress paths of
cmd_insert_cols, cmd_insert_rows, cmd_selection_colrow_hide,
cmd_paste_copy, cmd_shift_rows, cmd_shift_cols, and the filter undo.

This routes the four error notices through the control's GOCmdContext
(wb_control_error_message), the two yes/no questions through a new
WorkbookControlClass slot (query_yes_no, with wb_control_query_yes_no
returning the default answer when a control has no handler), and the
progress text through go_cmd_context_progress_message_set.  WBCGtk
implements the slot with go_gtk_query_yes_no and its command context
already shows notices and progress text the same way, so the GTK front
end behaves exactly as before.

Written against GNUMERIC_1_12_62; applied by scripts/build-gnumeric.sh to
the build copy (never to the submodule).  Upstream engagement is deferred
(docs/decisions.md ADR-011); the change is kept in upstreamable form.

